sn2.17:2.1 starts: “Constantly troubled is this mind,
sn2.17:2.2 starts: constantly trembling this heart,
sn2.17:2.3 starts: over duties that have yet to arise,
sn2.17:2.4 starts: and those already arisen.
sn2.17:2.5 starts: If there is an Untroubled,
sn2.17:2.6 starts: point it out to me, when asked.”
sn2.23:2.1 starts: “Truly, they delight in food,
sn2.23:2.2 starts: both devas & human beings,
sn2.23:2.3 starts: so what is the spirit
sn2.23:2.4 starts: who doesn’t delight in food?”
sn3.1:10.1 starts: For if it gains sustenance,
sn3.1:10.2 starts: becoming a great mass of flame,
sn3.1:10.3 starts: it may someday burn the fool,
sn3.1:10.4 starts: whether woman or man.
sn3.1:10.5 starts: So, guarding your life,
sn3.1:10.6 starts: avoid it.
sn2.22:3.1 starts: It’s not good,
sn2.22:3.2 starts: that, once it’s done,
sn2.22:3.3 starts: whose result you reap crying,
sn2.22:3.4 starts: your face in tears.
sn2.22:4.1 starts: It’s good,
sn2.22:4.2 starts: that, once it’s done,
sn2.22:4.3 starts: whose result you reap gratified,
sn2.22:4.4 starts: happy at heart.
sn2.25:6.1 starts: Those who live heedlessly:
sn2.25:6.2 starts: My words touch on them.
sn2.25:6.3 starts: Those who live heedfully:
sn2.25:6.4 starts: I pay them homage.
sn2.26:6.1 starts: It’s not to be reached by traveling,
sn2.26:6.2 starts: the end of the cosmos—
sn2.26:6.3 starts: And it’s not without reaching
sn2.26:6.4 starts: that there is release
sn3.1:6.1 starts: For it’s possible
sn3.1:6.2 starts: this noble warrior,
sn3.1:6.3 starts: and, angered at that disparagement,
sn3.1:6.4 starts: come down harshly
sn3.1:6.5 starts: So, guarding your life,
sn3.1:6.6 starts: avoid him.
sn3.1:7.1 starts: You shouldn’t look down on
sn3.1:7.2 starts: —for being young—
sn3.1:7.3 starts: a serpent you meet
sn3.1:7.4 starts: A person shouldn’t disparage it.
sn3.1:8.1 starts: As that potent snake slithers along
sn3.1:8.2 starts: with vibrant colors,
sn3.1:8.3 starts: it may someday burn the fool,
sn3.1:8.4 starts: whether woman or man.
sn3.1:8.5 starts: So,
sn3.1:8.6 starts: guarding your life,
sn3.1:9.1 starts: You shouldn’t look down on
sn3.1:9.2 starts: a blaze that feeds on many things,
sn3.1:9.3 starts: a flame with its blackened trail:
sn3.1:9.4 starts: A person shouldn’t disparage it.
sn3.1:13.1 starts: So a person who’s wise,
sn3.1:13.2 starts: out of regard for his own good,
sn3.1:13.3 starts: should always show due respect
sn3.1:13.4 starts: a serpent,
sn3.1:13.5 starts: a noble warrior with high status,
sn3.1:13.6 starts: & a monk, his virtue consummate.”
sn3.9:5.1 starts: Where goats, rams, & cattle
sn3.9:5.2 starts: of various kinds are killed:
sn3.9:5.3 starts: Those of right conduct, great seers,
sn3.9:5.4 starts: don’t attend that sacrifice.
sn3.9:6.1 starts: But sacrifices free from violence,
sn3.9:6.2 starts: offered always in line with family custom,
sn3.9:6.3 starts: where goats, rams, & cattle
sn3.9:6.4 starts: of various kinds are not killed:
sn3.9:6.5 starts: Those of right conduct, great seers,
sn3.9:6.6 starts: attend that sacrifice.
